Hmm, actually — alternatively I could avoid the symbol-on-handler approach altogether and avoid core changes: the adapter could track versioned routes in `applyVersionFilter` if it knew method+path... What if the election doesn't need registration-time tracking at all? 

Alternative: at request time, inspect `this.instance.router.stack` to find sibling versioned handlers? The layers contain the registered route path and the handle (the wrapper). If wrappers carry the symbol (they do when registered directly), we could build the registry lazily from the express router stack on first request. But with onRouteTriggered wrappers, layers' handles lack symbols again. Same problem.

OK, do the core symbol-forwarding. Actually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe simpler to have core attach the version metadata as Reflect metadata? No — keep symbols, forward in core.

